 "byline": "David Thrane Christiansen \u00b7 Lean FRO, 2023 (CC BY 4.0); this PDF is a browser print of the online book",
 "note": "The PDF is a 347-page print that stops partway through \u201cProgramming with Dependent Types\u201d (the online book has 461 printed pages). The tactics interlude and the chapter on programming, proving and performance are therefore missing. Per-chapter \u201cSummary\u201d pages are not broken out. Summaries are in our own words; the text stays in the PDF.",
 "summary": "An introduction to Lean 4 as a general-purpose functional programming language, for programmers who want to write real programs rather than proofs. It covers expressions, types, structures, inductive datatypes and polymorphism; compiling and running programs with IO and Lake; type classes, coercions and instance search; monads and do-notation; functors, applicative functors and universes; monad transformers and imperative-style do features; and programming with dependent types and indexed families.",
